# Copy to `.env` in the project root and adjust. Vite loads this for the dev server and build.
# Never commit a real token; `.env` is gitignored.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub (optional)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub Client ID for Device Flow. Required for in-app login.
# Create a GitHub App or OAuth App with "Device Flow" enabled.
# GITHUB_DEVICE_CLIENT_ID=

# Personal access token (classic or fine-grained) for Octokit. When set, it takes
# precedence over the token stored in the app (Settings). Leave empty to use
# only in-app / device sign-in. See https://github.com/settings/tokens
# VITE_GITHUB_TOKEN=
#
# Baked into the client bundle at `vite build` if present — do not set this
# in CI for release builds you ship; use Settings in the app instead.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tauri + Vite dev (optional)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# When set, the Vite dev server binds to this host instead of localhost-only, and HMR
# uses it. Use for development on another machine or device on your LAN (see Tauri docs).
# Example: TAURI_DEV_HOST=192.168.1.10
# TAURI_DEV_HOST=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vite / client (optional — only if you add `VITE_*` usage in `src/`)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Values must be prefixed with VITE_ to be exposed to the frontend as import.meta.env.VITE_*.
# VITE_PUBLIC_API_URL=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tooling (usually set by CI or scripts, not committed)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NODE_ENV=development
# CI=
